Bicep: use Microsoft.DocumentDB/databaseAccounts resource, e.g.
resource docdb 'Microsoft.DocumentDB/databaseAccounts@2021-04-15' = {
  name: 'myDocDbAccount'
  location: resourceGroup().location
  properties: {
    databaseAccountOfferType: 'Standard'
    capabilities: [ { name: 'EnableMongo' } ]
  }
}
Terraform (azurerm): azurerm_cosmosdb_account. Example block: resource "azurerm_cosmosdb_account" "docdb" { name = "myDocDbAccount" resource_group_name = azurerm_resource_group.rg.name location = azurerm_resource_group.rg.location offer_type = "Standard" kind = "MongoDB" consistency_policy { } }

Use a $geoNear aggregation stage as the pipeline's first stage. Example:
{ $geoNear: { near: { type: 'Point', coordinates: [ <lon>, <lat> ] }, distanceField: 'dist.calculated', maxDistance: <radiusMeters>, spherical: true } }
Then project/populate openingHours and stock fields and sort by dist.calculated.
